[38;5;252m[1m## Three issues found and fixed[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[38;5;252m[1m### 1. Wrong [38;5;10mdatalen[0m units in [38;5;10mgen_message_random[0m and [38;5;10mhash_message[0m (the core bug)[0m[0m
[0m[0m
In [38;5;10mhash.rs[0m, both [38;5;10mgen_message_random[0m and [38;5;10mhash_message[0m were multiplying the data length by 8 before passing it to [38;5;10mblake512_update[0m:[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1mrust
[0m[38;5;10m// WRONG — Rust was passing bit counts
blake512_update(&mut s, &sk_prf[..SPX_N], (SPX_N as u64) * 8);
[0m[0m[0m
[0m[0m
But the C code in [38;5;10mhash_blake.c[0m passes [1mbyte counts[22m directly:[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1mc
[0m[38;5;10m// C passes byte counts, NOT bit counts
blakeX_update(&S, sk_prf, SPX_N);
[0m[0m[0m
[0m[0m
The [38;5;10mblake512_update[0m function internally treats its [38;5;10mdatalen[0m parameter as [1mbits[22m (it does [38;5;10mdatalen >> 3[0m to get bytes). The standalone [38;5;10mblake512()[0m wrapper does the [38;5;10m*8[0m conversion, but [38;5;10mgen_message_random[0m and [38;5;10mhash_message[0m in C call [38;5;10mblake512_update[0m directly with raw byte counts — this is the actual C behavior that the test vectors were generated from.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
The translator incorrectly "fixed" this by adding the [38;5;10m*8[0m multiplication, but the correct translation must match the C behavior exactly, even if the C code appears to pass the wrong units.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1mFix:[22m Removed the [38;5;10m* 8[0m multiplications in both functions.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[38;5;252m[1m### 2. Missing exported symbol [38;5;10mSPX_gen_message_random[0m[0m[0m
[0m[0m
The test harness loads the shared library and looks up [38;5;10mSPX_gen_message_random[0m (the C uses [38;5;10mSPX_NAMESPACE(gen_message_random)[0m which expands to [38;5;10mSPX_gen_message_random[0m). The Rust [38;5;10mlib.rs[0m didn't export this symbol.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1mFix:[22m Added a [38;5;10m#[no_mangle] pub extern "C" fn SPX_gen_message_random(...)[0m wrapper in [38;5;10mlib.rs[0m.[0m[0m
